{
  "$comment": [
    "WOLS cross-library round-trip matrix (inputs only).",
    "Each case is encrypted by one implementation and decrypted by another.",
    "The document for a case is specimens[specimen] with 'id' set to specimenId.",
    "It is the generator's input and, unless expectSpecimen is set, what the",
    "decrypted label MUST equal.",
    "pbkdf2 cases: encrypt with 'passphrase'; every entry of decryptPassphrases MUST",
    "decrypt; every entry of rejectPassphrases MUST fail authentication. Omitted",
    "'iterations' means the library default; expectIterations is what the label must carry.",
    "raw cases: 'key' is the 32-byte key, base64url without padding.",
    "url cases: 'sig', when present, is attached as the sig parameter. The raw sig",
    "value in the URL MUST percent-decode (UTF-8, '+' literal) to it, and the decoder",
    "MUST return it unchanged. expectPathSegment, when present, is the exact",
    "percent-encoded ID path segment the generator must emit.",
    "fields cases: 'fields' are encrypted with field-level encryption.",
    "expectSpecimen, when present, names the document a WOLS 1.4.0 generator writes",
    "for the input and that every decoder MUST return (strain.generation: the JSON",
    "integer 1 in, the string \"1\" out). With legacyPlaintext, a label that carries",
    "the input unchanged (as the 1.3.0 releases wrote it) is also accepted on the",
    "wire, is reported as legacy, and MUST still decode to expectSpecimen.",
    "expectedFailures lists known divergences (optionally scoped by generator/decoder",
    "language). A listed case that passes is reported as an error, so fixed",
    "divergences must be removed from the list.",
    "This file is ASCII-only on purpose: non-NFC strings are written as \\u escapes."
  ],
